					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/adam-smascher" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(587467); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=587467&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609904802" alt="Adam Smascher" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=587467)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/adam-smascher" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(587467); return false;" >Adam Smascher</a></span> <span class="odate time_1297601763 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Feb 2011 12:56</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1001197">
									

<p>It's not a meme, though. This falls under the umbrella of "weird mind shit". This is <em>not</em> an idea of any kind.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The vector for SCP-405 is the subject's final mental vocalisation, identified by most observers as a "Death Scream." This vocalisation occurs at the moment of death, regardless of cause, and has a range of at least 200&nbsp;m, although the more advanced the disease the greater the range. Individuals who hear this telepathic signal are infected with SCP-405.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This right here, this mechanism of spread completely precludes it being memetic.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Addendum 405-01: Request use of SCP-148 in containment rooms. -Agent ██████<br />
Denied, SCP-148 stocks are low enough as it is and we can treat anyone caught in the radius of a SCP-405 termination. In addition <strong>memetic readings</strong> predict terminal phase activation is a strength ████ signal, requiring ██ of SCP-148 to shield. -O5-█</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Then there was telekill. What part of <em>THE GOGGLES DO NOTHING</em> is so hard to understand? Furthermore, what does memetic readings mean?</p>

